# Testing and Validation

## Testing Approach

The prototype was evaluated at hardware level using controlled/test inputs.

The purpose was to verify whether the ESP32 firmware correctly responded to different predefined conditions.

---

## Functional Test Cases

| Test | Input Condition | Expected Response | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| Safe | Normal sensor condition | Green LED + SAFE on LCD | PASS |
| Landslide | Vibration HIGH | Red LED + buzzer + LANDSLIDE alert | PASS |
| Heavy Rain | Rain level above threshold | Yellow LED + warning buzzer | PASS |
| SOS | SOS button activated | Red LED + fast buzzer + SOS alert | PASS |
| Blynk | Cloud connection | Dashboard/alert communication | PASS |
| ThingSpeak | Sensor data transmission | Time-series logging | PASS |

---

## Important Clarification

These tests verify the programmed system response using controlled/test inputs.

They do not represent long-term real-world environmental measurements collected from an actual hill location.

---

## Field Testing

Actual field deployment was not completed during the initial project presentation.

The evaluation feedback highlighted the importance of testing the vibration sensing mechanism in an actual soil/ground environment.

This is considered a next-stage validation activity.

---

## Proposed Field Test

A future field test should use:

1. A suitable ground/soil vibration sensor
2. A protective enclosure
3. Water-resistant sealing
4. Protected cable connections
5. ESP32 control unit
6. Data logging
7. Controlled vibration experiments
8. Long-duration environmental monitoring
